00:51:04,123 --> 00:51:06,785
At the sanatorium, they
conducted blood tests.

524
00:51:08,883 --> 00:51:12,418
The tests suggest that
the shadow you can see

525
00:51:12,443 --> 00:51:14,168
at the base of your skull

526
00:51:14,763 --> 00:51:16,203
is not cancer.

527
00:51:17,445 --> 00:51:19,005
It is tuberculoma.

528
00:51:21,596 --> 00:51:25,076
A tubercular growth caused
by the same bacteria as TB.

529
00:51:28,582 --> 00:51:30,613
You may have picked it
up from your daughter.

530
00:51:32,717 --> 00:51:36,278
Once this disease enters a
household, it can run wild.

531
00:51:37,065 --> 00:51:39,665
It can be transmitted
with a simple kiss.

532
00:51:43,669 --> 00:51:46,269
It seems the Shelby
household is no exception.

533
00:51:50,443 --> 00:51:54,483
Mr Shelby, as I say, I am aware
that you are still grieving,

534
00:51:55,723 --> 00:51:58,323
but you must understand
this is very serious.

535
00:52:00,563 --> 00:52:03,803
From the size of the tumour,
expansion must've been rapid.

536
00:52:05,118 --> 00:52:08,878
I have no doubt that you are
already experiencing symptoms?

537
00:52:10,573 --> 00:52:12,573
Have you recently
suffered seizures?

538
00:52:14,020 --> 00:52:19,580
Bouts of weakness,
dissociation, hallucinations?

539
00:52:27,683 --> 00:52:29,283
Why didn't you come and see me?

540
00:52:32,003 --> 00:52:33,203
I have work to do.

541
00:52:37,116 --> 00:52:38,596
Am I a danger to others?

542
00:52:40,395 --> 00:52:41,464
No.

543
00:52:42,123 --> 00:52:45,137
Unlike TB, tuberculoma
is not infectious.

544
00:52:45,877 --> 00:52:47,144
Mr Shelby,

545
00:52:47,894 --> 00:52:49,598
it is not infectious,

546
00:52:49,852 --> 00:52:51,316
but in your case.

547
00:52:52,150 --> 00:52:54,270
I am afraid it is inoperable.

548
00:52:56,132 --> 00:52:58,068
The growth is in
your brain stem.

549
00:52:58,163 --> 00:52:59,539
Any attempt to remove it

550
00:52:59,563 --> 00:53:02,003
would result in trauma
and brain haemorrhage.

551
00:53:06,606 --> 00:53:08,539
Whilst you were
refusing my calls,

552
00:53:08,563 --> 00:53:11,923
I showed your X-rays to three of
the best surgeons in the country.

553
00:53:15,843 --> 00:53:17,668
They all said they
would not operate

554
00:53:19,083 --> 00:53:20,443
as it would be futile.

555
00:53:22,123 --> 00:53:26,403
Of course, you will want a
second opinion for yourself.

556
00:53:27,603 --> 00:53:30,779
Doctor Helen Rutherford
at St Thomas'.

557
00:53:30,803 --> 00:53:32,123
She is a friend.

558
00:53:43,324 --> 00:53:44,363
This...

559
00:53:46,597 --> 00:53:47,957
How bad will it get?

560
00:53:54,411 --> 00:53:56,035
As the tumour grows,

561
00:53:56,745 --> 00:54:00,585
the rate of physical and mental
deterioration will increase.

562
00:54:05,045 --> 00:54:09,051
Eventually, you will need
people around you constantly,

563
00:54:09,883 --> 00:54:11,692
who love you very much.

564
00:54:14,859 --> 00:54:16,099
How long?

565
00:54:19,803 --> 00:54:23,082
I understand you have defeated
many enemies, Mr Shelby.

566
00:54:24,189 --> 00:54:25,604
Now, you have a new one

567
00:54:26,477 --> 00:54:27,757
inside you.

568
00:54:29,190 --> 00:54:30,630
You cannot defeat it,

569
00:54:32,203 --> 00:54:34,072
but you can keep it
at bay for a while.

570
00:54:34,899 --> 00:54:39,115
If you live correctly, if you are
determined and if you fight...

571
00:54:39,140 --> 00:54:40,689
I asked you a question.

572
00:54:41,091 --> 00:54:42,603
So, I want an answer.

573
00:54:42,763 --> 00:54:44,854
I don't want your
fucking platitudes.

574
00:54:45,603 --> 00:54:50,189
How long before I need people
around me, who love me very much?

575
00:54:55,018 --> 00:54:56,697
Sorry. It's fine, Lizzie.

576
00:54:56,861 --> 00:54:58,370
My accountant here
was just leaving.

577
00:55:04,443 --> 00:55:06,939
I will telephone you,
when I get back to London.

578
00:55:06,963 --> 00:55:08,268
No, I don't have enough time.

579
00:55:08,293 --> 00:55:10,314
You're an accountant, give
me a fucking number now.

580
00:55:12,364 --> 00:55:13,415
One year.

581
00:55:14,915 --> 00:55:16,282
Perhaps 18 months.

582
00:55:17,265 --> 00:55:19,158
That's fine. That's
all I need to know.

583
00:55:19,792 --> 00:55:22,846
I will adjust my finances
accordingly. Thank you.

584
00:55:25,083 --> 00:55:27,994
I will write to you, explaining the
full implications. Yeah, thank you.

585
00:55:32,563 --> 00:55:33,822
Good day.

586
00:55:42,393 --> 00:55:43,830
Something serious?

587
00:55:45,043 --> 00:55:46,721
No, no, just a

588
00:55:47,931 --> 00:55:50,290
just a bill I wasn't
expecting and I...

589
00:55:51,420 --> 00:55:53,020
I'll have to pay it.

590
00:56:02,806 --> 00:56:04,658
Will you give me a
minute on my own, Lizzie?

591
00:56:08,923 --> 00:56:09,979
Yeah.

592
00:56:25,823 --> 00:56:27,025
Not a devil

593
00:56:30,269 --> 00:56:31,993
just an ordinary mortal man.

594
00:56:38,843 --> 00:56:41,346
There will be a
war in this family,

595
00:56:43,183 --> 00:56:45,023
and one of you will die.

596
00:56:47,603 --> 00:56:49,123
Polly.

597
00:56:50,813 --> 00:56:53,413
Just give me enough time
to do what I have to do.

598
00:56:55,683 --> 00:56:57,099
Kill.

599
00:56:57,123 --> 00:56:58,883
Kill.

